[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 4. **Calculate the perimeter of one of the triangles:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m    Since the median of a triangle is half the length of the hypotenuse, the perimeter of one of the triangles is the sum of the lengths of the two sides of the triangle. The two sides of the triangle are the two sides of the original square, which are each 7 inches. Therefore, the perimeter of one of the triangles is:
