[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m (n-1)n(n+1) = 120
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m We need to find the value of \( n \) such that the product is 120. Let's test some values of \( n \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 1. If \( n = 4 \), then the product is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m (4-1) \cdot 4 \cdot (4+1) = 3 \cdot 4 \cdot 5 = 60
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m This is not 120.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 2. If \( n = 5 \), then the product is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m (5-1) \cdot 5 \cdot (5+1) = 4 \cdot 5 \cdot 6 = 120
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \]
