[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m [response]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m  To solve for \(a\) and \(b\) in the polynomial \(p(x) = x^2 + ax + b\) given that it has distinct roots \(2a\) and \(b\), we can use the fact that for a quadratic polynomial with roots \(p\) and \(q\), the polynomial can be written as \((x - p)(x - q) = x^2 - (p+q)x + pq\). Here, the roots are \(2a\) and \(b\), so we can identify \(p = 2a\) and \(q = b\). Therefore, the polynomial can be written as:
