[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m [response] To solve the problem, let's denote the three consecutive integers as \( n-1 \), \( n \), and \( n+1 \). The product of these integers is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m (n-1)n(n+1) = 120
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m We can expand and simplify this equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \[
