[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m where \(\theta\) is the angle between the vectors \(\mathbf{v}\) and \(\mathbf{w}\). Given that \(\|\mathbf{v}\| = 3\) and \(\|\mathbf{w}\| = 4\), we need to find the minimum value of \(\cos \theta\). The cosine of the angle \(\theta\) between two vectors is maximized when the vectors are in the same direction, and minimized when the vectors are in opposite directions. Therefore, the minimum value of \(\cos \theta\) is \(-1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
