[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m [response] To find the volume of the cube, we first need to determine the side length of the cube. The volume of a sphere is given by the formula \(V = \frac{4}{3} \pi r^3\), where \(r\) is the radius of the sphere. The radius of the sphere inscribed in the cube is half the side length of the cube, so if the volume of the sphere is \(\frac{\pi}{6}\) cubic inches, then the volume of the cube is \(3\) times the volume of the sphere.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m Let's denote the side length of the cube by \(s\). The radius of the sphere is \(\frac{s}{2}\), so the volume of the sphere is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m V_{\text{sphere}} = \frac{4}{3} \pi \left(\frac{s}{2}\right)^3 = \frac{4}{3} \pi \frac{s^3}{8} = \frac{\pi s^3}{6}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m \]
