[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 2. **Understand the folding process:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m    When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, the resulting triangle is congruent to one of the original triangles formed by the fold. The fold line is the perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining the opposite corners of the original square. This fold line is also the median of the original square, which is 7 inches long.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=6911)[0m 3. **Calculate the area of one of the congruent triangles:**
